1 0 0 1 72 760 Tm (Synthetic AUTOSAR-Style HLD Demonstration Document) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 746 Tm (Document: Vehicle Lighting Controller HLD) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 732 Tm (Notice: This document is synthetic demonstration data only.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 718 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 704 Tm (Page 1. System Overview) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm (The Vehicle Lighting Controller is a fictional high-level design for a simple) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 676 Tm (exterior lighting feature. The Light Control application component receives) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 662 Tm (driver lighting requests and decides whether the headlamp command should be ON) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 648 Tm (or OFF. The component that controls the exterior lamp decision is Light Control.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 634 Tm (The Vehicle Signal Interface component adapts vehicle network values) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 620 Tm (into application-level signals for the Light Control component.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 606 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 592 Tm (Identified components:) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 578 Tm (- Light Control application component) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 564 Tm (- Vehicle Signal Interface component) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 550 Tm (- Lamp Driver Interface component) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 536 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 522 Tm (The design goal is to show traceable document question answering with source) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 508 Tm (pages, not to define a certified automotive architecture.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 1131 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 760 Tm (Page 2. Interfaces, Ports, and Signals) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 746 Tm (The Light Control application component has a required port named) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 732 Tm (R_HeadlampSwitch. This port receives the input signal HeadlampSwitchRequest from) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 718 Tm (the Vehicle Signal Interface component.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 704 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm (The Light Control application component has a provided port named P_LampStatus.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 676 Tm (This port publishes the output signal LampStatus for diagnostic display and) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 662 Tm (operator feedback. LampStatus can report OFF, LOW_BEAM_ON, or FAULT_DETECTED in) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 648 Tm (this synthetic example. The signal that reports lamp status is LampStatus.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 634 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 620 Tm (The interface I_LightCommand carries the internal command LightCommand from the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 606 Tm (Light Control application component to the Lamp Driver Interface component. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 592 Tm (Lamp Driver Interface converts LightCommand into a hardware-oriented lamp drive) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 578 Tm (request.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 1641 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
14 TL
1 0 0 1 72 760 Tm (Page 3. Dependencies and Functional Flow) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 746 Tm (The Light Control application component depends on HeadlampSwitchRequest being) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 732 Tm (available from the Vehicle Signal Interface component. It also depends on the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 718 Tm (Lamp Driver Interface accepting the LightCommand signal.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 704 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 690 Tm (Functional flow:) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 676 Tm (1. Vehicle Signal Interface reads HeadlampSwitchRequest from a fictional) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 662 Tm (vehicle network source.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 648 Tm (2. Light Control evaluates HeadlampSwitchRequest. If the request is ON and no) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 634 Tm (fault condition is present, Light Control sets LightCommand to LOW_BEAM_ON.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 620 Tm (3. Lamp Driver Interface receives LightCommand and issues a lamp drive request.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 606 Tm (4. Light Control publishes LampStatus so a display or diagnostic function can) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 592 Tm (show the current lamp state.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 578 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 564 Tm (Architecture decision:) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 550 Tm (The signal adaptation responsibility is kept in Vehicle Signal Interface so the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 536 Tm (Light Control component does not depend directly on network frame details.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 522 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 72 508 Tm (Safety note:) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 494 Tm (This sample is for academic demonstration only. Real vehicle lighting behavior,) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 480 Tm (safety analysis, fault handling, and production changes require qualified human) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 466 Tm (review and project-specific engineering evidence.) Tj
ET
endstream
